  "interpretation": "The normalized observable sensitivity matrix (S_obs) exhibited numerical rank 6 out of 16 parameters (rank fraction 0.38) under the relative threshold 0.0001. The condition number was \u03ba = 656.1, indicating limited local distinguishability for the evaluated parameter subset under the tested operating conditions.\n\nSeveral parameter pairs exhibited high absolute cosine similarity (|cos(\u03b8)| \u2265 0.95): (mineralization_rate, mineralization_efficiency, |cos|=1.000); (growth_yield, biomass_nutrient_content, |cos|=1.000); (damage_rate, repair_rate, |cos|=1.000); (maximum_uptake_rate, q10_coefficient, |cos|=1.000); (repair_rate, osmotic_half_effect, |cos|=1.000). These parameters may be locally confounded under the available observable set, limiting independent parameter recovery for those pairs.\n\nPerturbation convergence analysis showed stable sensitivity estimates across all evaluated perturbation fractions, supporting the local character of the finite-difference approximation.\n\nIMPORTANT: This analysis characterises local sensitivity at the benchmark's nominal operating point. It provides evidence of local practical identifiability for the evaluated subset under the tested conditions. It does NOT establish structural or global identifiability, and it does not guarantee parameter recoverability from real experimental data subject to measurement noise."
